# L §8.4: "A refusal propagates like a hole and outranks it."  normal(mu[k2], sd) with sd = -5 is RUN-PARAM (L §5.16)
# though mu[k2] is a hole (no row: HOLE-UNGOVERNED with the input's question, L §4.6 step 5): q and q2 are refused.
# none in arithmetic, max or an ordering is RUN-NONE (L §3.1) whatever the hole beside it holds (y1, y2, y3, y5);
# sqrt(-1) is RUN-DOMAIN beside a hole (y4); pow(hole, -1) may be anything, a division by zero included, so it stays
# the hole (y6).
=== m.tally
model p12
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-18
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"

index ks = [k1, k2]

input mu[k in ks]: num question "what is mu?"
input sd: num
input nn: num
input z: num

def x[k in ks]: dist = normal(mu[k], sd) to 1e-6
def y1[k in ks]: num = mu[k] + nn
def y2[k in ks]: num = nn * mu[k]
def y3[k in ks]: num = max(mu[k], nn)
def y4[k in ks]: num = sqrt(mu[k]) to 1e-6 + sqrt(z) to 1e-6
def y5[k in ks]: bool = mu[k] < nn
def y6[k in ks]: num = pow(mu[k], z) to 1e-6

ask q: mean(x[k2])
ask q2: cdf(x[k2], z)
ask q3: y1[k2], y2[k2], y3[k2], y4[k2], y5[k2], y6[k2]

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  mu[k1] = 1
  sd = -5
  nn = none
  z = -1
=== expect
q: refused: RUN-PARAM normal parameter s = -5 is invalid
  cut 2026-10-18
q2: refused: RUN-PARAM normal parameter s = -5 is invalid
  cut 2026-10-18
q3: (refused: RUN-NONE a value is none here: arithmetic, refused: RUN-NONE a value is none here: arithmetic, refused: RUN-NONE a value is none here: max, refused: RUN-DOMAIN sqrt(-1) outside its domain, refused: RUN-NONE a value is none here: an ordering, ?"what is mu?" (mu[k2]))
  cut 2026-10-18
